### Please describe the problem in your own words.

The `remote.proxy-target.annex-readonly` configuration does not prevent modifications to the proxy-target remote if it is accessed via a proxy.

### What steps will reproduce the problem?

[[!format sh """
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euxo pipefail

# Set up an empty proxy target repository
mkdir target
cd target
git init
git annex init
cd ..

# Set up the proxying repository
mkdir proxy
cd proxy
git init
git annex init
echo test0 > test0.txt
git annex add .
git commit -m commit
# Add proxy target remote, make it readonly, and enable proxying
git remote add target ../target
git config remote.target.annex-readonly true
git config remote.target.annex-proxy true
git annex updateproxy
# Check that the readonly configuration is effective
set +e
git annex move --to target
set -e
cd ..

# Make a clone of the proxying repository
git clone ssh://$USER@localhost$PWD/proxy clone
cd clone
git annex init
# Add some new annexed content
echo test1 > test1.txt
echo test2 > test2.txt
git annex add .
git commit -m commit2
# Modify the proxy target, even though it is configured to be readonly
git annex move --to origin-target
git annex move --from origin-target
cd ..
"""]]

